  "note": "The closing fee is a fixed rupee amount per price band, crossed with a lettered group that decides which amount a fee category pays in the two lowest bands. Group membership read from the section's own group lists: 'Apparel - Shirts' and 'Kitchen - Cookware, Tableware & Dinnerware' are in Group # (0-300) and Group ## (301-500); 'Accessories - Electronics, PC and Wireless' is in Group A (0-300) and Group C (301-500). None of the three is in the '*' list that pays the higher above-1000 amount, so all three take the standard above-1000 fee. The band bounds are read on the page's own basis, on every rule below as slab_basis: the \"item price that is paid by the buyer (including any shipping or gift-wrap charges charged by the seller)\", not the seller's pre-tax principal and not the order total.",
